# Irreducible pairing for the external cubic component

The genuine generalized-Fitting product gives the joint-centralizer bound
and a two-group quotient by `KX`. An actual nontrivial component constituent
is classified by H.6.1. Its extension to the full group or to the index-two
inner-action preimage lets cubic Clifford theory determine multiplicity two.
The result is an actual intertwining equivalence with two Steinberg modules
or two natural-dual pairs, with the H.6.1 input also discharged by its proved
concrete catalogue.

The joint-centralizer bound does not require full conjugation image and also
applies to the compatible SL₃(2) × S₃ configuration. Assembly on all literal
chief sections belongs to the chief-decomposition theorem.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith 13.8.21(1), printed p.956.
-/
